g pathways including Hippo, MAPK, nuclear receptor and cytoskeleton remodeling (PubMed:32640226). Different types of STRIPAK complexes are involved in a variety of biological processes such as cell growth, differentiation, apoptosis, metabolism and immune regulation (Probable). Key regulator of the expanded Hippo signaling pathway by interacting and allowing the inhibition of MAP4K kinases by the STRIPAK complex (PubMed:32640226)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}